		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Bullet Showcase Contest, win a Playstation 3 or Nintendo Wii]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=2749#p2749"><![CDATA[
A Bullet Physics Showcase Contest will start, getting some showcases for free open source physics software. Prizes include the new Playstation 3 and a Nintendo Wii console.<br><br>Rules are simple:<br>Use latest Bullet Physics SDK, integrate it into a graphics engine, or other application, and impress with a good looking physics effect. Use of COLLADA Physics is a bonus.<br><br>Deadline is before GDC 2007, more details follow.<br><br>Just post here if you are interested:<br><a href="http://continuousphysics.com/Bullet/phpBB2/viewforum.php?f=17" class="postlink">http://continuousphysics.com/Bullet/php ... m.php?f=17</a><br><br>Erwin<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Fri Dec 08, 2006 11:38 pm</p><hr />
